| !Run for !OpenTTD - RISC OS port of OpenTTD 14.1
| Built with GCCSDK GCC 10.2 (arm-riscos-gnueabihf), statically linked.

Set OpenTTD$Dir <Obey$Dir>
IconSprites <OpenTTD$Dir>.!Sprites
| Sprite for the icon bar icon shown while the game runs in a window.
Set SDL$IconSprite !openttd

| --- Runtime support -------------------------------------------------
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 IfThere System:Modules.SharedULib Then RMLoad System:Modules.SharedULib
RMEnsure SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 Error OpenTTD needs SharedUnixLibrary 1.16 or later. Install it with PackMan.
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 IfThere System:Modules.ARMEABISupport Then RMLoad System:Modules.ARMEABISupport
RMEnsure ARMEABISupport 0 Error OpenTTD needs the ARMEABISupport module. Install it with PackMan.
If "<Alias$@RunType_E1F>"="" Then Error OpenTTD needs !SharedLibs to run ELF programs. Install SharedLibs with PackMan and make sure the Filer has seen it.

| --- Sound (optional; needs DigitalRenderer) -----------------------
Set OpenTTD$Sound -s sdl
RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 IfThere System:Modules.DRenderer Then RMLoad System:Modules.DRenderer
RMEnsure DigitalRenderer 0.51 Set OpenTTD$Sound -s null

| --- Memory ---------------------------------------------------------
| The C heap lives in a dynamic area called "OpenTTD Heap" (up to 512MB),
| which is removed when the game quits.
WimpSlot -min 32768K -max 32768K
| --- Display ---------------------------------------------------------
| OpenTTD$Display: "fullscreen" (switches to a screen mode of that size)
|                  or "windowed" (a desktop window of that size).
| OpenTTD$Size:    width x height, e.g. 1280x720. Smaller runs faster.
Unset OpenTTD$Display
Unset OpenTTD$Size
| Default: a 1024x768 desktop window. Put a | in front of these two lines
| to use the choices from Game Options > Graphics instead.
Set OpenTTD$Display windowed
Set OpenTTD$Size 1024x768
| In a high resolution desktop mode (EX0 EY0, "180dpi") the window is
| drawn at double size so it looks the same as in a 90dpi mode. To turn
| that off, or to force a scale, remove the | from this line (1 = off,
| 2 to 4 = scale).
Unset SDL$WindowScale
| Set SDL$WindowScale 1
Set OpenTTD$Video sdl
If "<OpenTTD$Display>"<>"" Then Do Set OpenTTD$Video sdl:<OpenTTD$Display>
Unset OpenTTD$Res
If "<OpenTTD$Size>"<>"" Then Do Set OpenTTD$Res -r <OpenTTD$Size>

| --- Program -------------------------------------------------------
| openttd-fast is built for the NEON instructions of the Raspberry Pi 2
| and later (and other Cortex-A machines) and is used when it's there.
| To use the standard build instead, put a | in front of the IfThere line.
Set OpenTTD$Binary openttd
IfThere <OpenTTD$Dir>.openttd-fast Then Set OpenTTD$Binary openttd-fast

| -b 32bpp-optimized is the quickest blitter (no water/light animation);
| use -b 32bpp-anim for animation.
| "Do" expands the <variables> before the command runs (Run does not).
Do Run <OpenTTD$Dir>.<OpenTTD$Binary> -v <OpenTTD$Video> <OpenTTD$Res> -b 32bpp-optimized -m null <OpenTTD$Sound> %*0 2><Wimp$ScrapDir>.OpenTTDlog
